      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: show provider plan usage (5h/weekly/credits) in the chat context popover, keep API cost for API billing",
        "body": "Closes #102771\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Anthropic subscription users (Claude Pro/Max via the `claude-cli` backend or `anthropic` OAuth) saw only meaningless dollar tiles (`Est. cost $0.020`, `Cost by type $0.00`) in the chat composer's context popover, with no plan usage at all. Two gaps: `claude-cli`-only setups never resolved a usage fetcher (`resolveUsageProviderId(\"claude-cli\")` had no mapping, so usage loading ended in `Unsupported provider`), and even for providers with usage windows (Codex OAuth) the popover reduced everything to a single \"Usage Remaining 28%\" pill with no per-window breakdown, reset times, credits, or plan label.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSubscription billing is bounded by plan windows, not per-token dollars — the popover should show the numbers that actually constrain the user (like CodexBar does). The change routes `claude-cli` into the existing Anthropic usage pipeline (usage id mapping + a plugin-owned OAuth fallback to the synced `claude-cli` profile), carries `plan` (from the Claude CLI keychain's `subscriptionType`/`rateLimitTier`, e.g. `Max (20x)`) and `billing` (extra-usage credits) through `models.authStatus`, and redesigns the popover: per-window bars (5-hour, weekly, model-scoped) with reset times and severity coloring, a usage-credits row, and a link to the Usage page. Sessions whose provider is plan-billed hide the dollar estimates; API-billed sessions keep `Est. cost` and cost-by-type unchanged. Identical usage exposed through both `anthropic` and `claude-cli` auth rows collapses to one group. The duplicate \"Extra usage\" window is dropped at the fetcher when the budget billing entry exists.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Claude subscription users see 5-hour / weekly / model-scoped plan usage with reset times, plan label, and usage credits directly in the chat popover; `claude-cli`-only setups (Claude Code keychain login) now surface usage on the popover, the Usage page, and the models dashboard (previously nothing).\n- API-key users keep the existing per-token cost breakdown.\n- Codex OAuth users get the same bar treatment for their 5h/weekly windows.\n\nScreenshots (mock-gateway Playwright harness):\n\n| Claude subscription | Codex OAuth |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![claude](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/context-popover-plan-usage/claude-subscription-popover.png) | ![codex](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/context-popover-plan-usage/codex-popover.png) |\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Testbox (delegated, exit 0): focused suites `src/infra/provider-usage.shared.test.ts`, `src/infra/provider-usage.fetch.claude.test.ts`, `extensions/anthropic/usage.test.ts`, `src/agents/cli-credentials.test.ts`, `src/gateway/server-methods/models-auth-status.test.ts`, `ui/src/lib/provider-quota-summary.test.ts`, `ui/src/pages/chat/chat-composer.test.ts`, `ui/src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts`, `src/agents/auth-profiles.external-cli-sync.test.ts`, `src/agents/auth-profiles.external-cli-scope.test.ts`, plus mocked-gateway e2e `ui/src/e2e/chat-quota-pill-93041.e2e.test.ts` (3 tests incl. new subscription scenario) and `ui/src/e2e/chat-composer-redesign.e2e.test.ts`.\n- New tests: claude-cli→anthropic usage id mapping; anthropic usage auth falls back to the synced claude-cli OAuth profile; plan label formatting (`max`/`default_max_20x` → `Max (20x)`); billing passthrough on `models.authStatus`; quota group dedupe/clamping; subscription popover hides `Est. cost`/cost-by-type while API sessions keep them; extra-usage window kept only when credit amounts are missing.\n- `pnpm ui:i18n:sync` regenerated locale bundles for the new popover strings.\n- Docs: `docs/concepts/usage-tracking.md` gained the chat-popover surface entry.\n",
        "branch": "claude/cost-control-redesign-25946d",
